    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I've noticed that sometimes when playing in certain registers, there seem to be these slight, almost unidentifiable frequencies that don't quite fit the main harmonic series—they almost sound like they're 'hiding' under the main note. Are those just artifacts of the physics, or is there a more technical way to categorize those subtle, unexpected sounds?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
